      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name} The main reason this comes to mind really is prefabs. Systems like Audiolink, video players, Openflight, etc, can really benefit from being searchable tags. For example, if you go here https://vrchat.com/home/search/openflight then you can see all the worlds that either users have tagged that use my prefab or that my auto-tagging script has asked them to add the correct tag. The issue is theres plenty of worlds not listed on there that just cant add the tag because they were at the tag limit since basically day 1 of them uploading the world due to how small the limit is. Same applys for Audiolink, if your trying to find worlds that specifically have that, you might miss some really good worlds if the creator doesnt tag them or just doesnt have the space to do so in their tags. A direct world example is this one, which I know has OpenFlight in it, but the tags that they already have there are also extremely relevant to the world, so theres not much they can do. https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_4b341546-65ff-4607-9d38-5b7f8f405132",
